🟡 Intermediate SQL for Data Engineers
✅ Topics
LEFT, RIGHT, FULL OUTER JOIN

Subqueries and CTEs

CASE statements

Window functions (ROW_NUMBER, RANK, LAG, LEAD)

UNION and INTERSECT

Data constraints and indexing basics

🛠️ Project Ideas
Project	Description
Sales Funnel Analysis	Use window functions to rank leads and analyze conversion stages.
Data Cleaning Pipeline	Build a CTE-based pipeline to clean and transform messy data.
Product Performance Dashboard	Use JOINs and subqueries to calculate KPIs like average order value, top-selling products.
🔴 Advanced SQL for Data Engineers
✅ Topics
Recursive CTEs

Query optimization (EXPLAIN plans, indexing)

Stored procedures and triggers

Transactions and ACID properties

Partitioning and sharding

Star and snowflake schemas

SQL in cloud platforms (BigQuery, Redshift, Snowflake)

🛠️ Project Ideas
Project	Description
Hierarchical Data Modeling	Use recursive CTEs to model org charts or category trees.
Data Warehouse Design	Build a star schema for a retail analytics system.
Performance Tuning Lab	Compare query speeds with and without indexes, and analyze EXPLAIN plans.
Cloud SQL Integration	Load and query large datasets in BigQuery or Snowflake using advanced SQL.
🧭 How to Progress
Start with basic SQL on small datasets (CSV files, SQLite, MySQL).

Move to intermediate SQL with real business logic (ETL, dashboards).

Advance into performance, scalability, and cloud integration — this is where data engineering shines.



